---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Privacy Blur for Teams"
  description="Privacy policy for Privacy Blur for Teams Chrome extension. Learn what data we collect, what stays local, and how we protect your privacy."
  canonical="https://amrita-labs.com/privacy-blur-teams/privacy/"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 prose prose-invert prose-sm">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">Privacy Policy — Privacy Blur for Teams</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400"><strong>Effective Date</strong>: 2026-07-22 · <strong>Last Updated</strong>: 2026-07-22</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Summary</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">Privacy Blur for Teams does <strong>not</strong> collect, store, or transmit any of your Teams messages, contact names, meeting notes, files, or personal data. The extension runs locally in your browser on <code>teams.cloud.microsoft</code>. No Teams content leaves your device.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Data We Do NOT Collect</h2>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Message content, sender names, conversation titles, or meeting chat text</li>
      <li>Files, screenshots, images, videos, or attachments shared in Teams</li>
      <li>Your Microsoft credentials, login tokens, or account details</li>
      <li>Browsing history or activity outside of <code>teams.cloud.microsoft</code></li>
      <li>Any personally identifiable information (PII) from your Teams workspace</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Data We Store Locally</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">The following is stored in <code>chrome.storage.sync</code> (synced across your Chrome browsers, never sent to our servers unless stated below for analytics or billing):</p>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Your blur zone preferences (which zones are enabled or disabled)</li>
      <li>Hover-to-reveal and blur intensity settings</li>
      <li>Custom keyword rules such as salary, OTP, or invoice</li>
      <li>Panel position and other local UI preferences</li>
      <li>Trial start timestamp and premium access state</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Analytics</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">We collect minimal, anonymous usage events via PostHog to understand which features are used and whether the extension is working reliably. Example events include <em>extension installed</em>, <em>blur toggled</em>, and <em>paywall viewed</em>. These events may contain:</p>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>A random anonymous ID generated by the extension</li>
      <li>Event name and basic product properties (for example, which zone was toggled)</li>
      <li>Extension version and coarse product metadata</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mt-4">We do <strong>not</strong> collect Teams message content, sender names, conversation titles, chat previews, or any text that identifies you or your organization.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Payments</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">Premium features are processed by <a href="https://extensionpay.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[#aab0ff] hover:underline">ExtensionPay</a> (powered by Stripe). We never see or store your payment card details. Stripe handles payment data under its own <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[#aab0ff] hover:underline">privacy policy</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Permissions</h2>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li><strong>storage</strong>: Save your blur preferences, keyword rules, and settings across sessions</li>
      <li><strong>host_permissions (teams.cloud.microsoft)</strong>: Inject the blur overlay on Microsoft Teams Web only</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Third-Party Services</h2>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li><strong>PostHog</strong> (anonymous analytics) — <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[#aab0ff] hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><strong>ExtensionPay / Stripe</strong> (payments) — <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[#aab0ff] hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Retention</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">Local preferences remain stored until you uninstall the extension or clear browser data. Anonymous analytics events are retained under our PostHog retention settings (currently up to 12 months) and then deleted or aggregated. Billing records are retained by ExtensionPay and Stripe according to their policies.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Rights</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">You can delete local extension data by uninstalling the extension or clearing extension storage. To request deletion of anonymous analytics data or ask a privacy question, contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@amrita-labs.com" class="text-[#aab0ff] hover:underline">hello@amrita-labs.com</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Changes</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted at this URL. Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">Amrita Labs<br />Email: <a href="mailto:hello@amrita-labs.com" class="text-[#aab0ff] hover:underline">hello@amrita-labs.com</a><br />Website: <a href="https://amrita-labs.com/privacy-blur-teams/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[#aab0ff] hover:underline">amrita-labs.com/privacy-blur-teams</a></p>
  </article>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-12 flex gap-6 text-xs text-gray-500">
    <a href="/privacy-blur-teams/" class="hover:text-gray-400">← Back to Privacy Blur for Teams</a>
  </div>
</Base>
